From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211_hwsim: keep radar detection on a multi-radio wiphy

A radio that uses channel contexts gets no radar detection widths in its
global interface combination, because DFS requires a combination with a
single channel. A multi-radio radio always uses channel contexts, and
its global combination multiplies the channel count by the number of
radios. So it loses the radar detection widths as well, while each
per-radio combination keeps them.

mac80211 checks the channel of a radar detection against the global
combination (ieee80211_check_combinations() with radio_idx -1 from
_ieee80211_link_use_channel()). No combination matches, and every CAC on
a multi-radio hwsim radio fails. hostapd reports it as "start_dfs_cac()
failed" and disables the interface.

cfg80211 exempts the global combination of a multi-radio wiphy from the
single channel rule for DFS (wiphy_verify_iface_combinations()), since
it only sums up the radios. Keep the radar detection widths there when
each radio has one channel. With more than one channel per radio, clear
them in the per-radio combination too, which cfg80211 would refuse
otherwise.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/mac80211_hwsim_main.c
@@ -6099,8 +6099,14 @@ static int mac80211_hwsim_new_radio(stru
 		data->if_combination.num_different_channels *= n_bands;
 	}
 
-	if (data->use_chanctx)
+	/*
+	 * DFS needs a single channel per combination. cfg80211 exempts the
+	 * global combination of a multi-radio wiphy.
+	 */
+	if (data->use_chanctx && (!param->multi_radio || data->channels > 1)) {
 		data->if_combination.radar_detect_widths = 0;
+		data->if_combination_radio.radar_detect_widths = 0;
+	}
 
 	/* By default all radios belong to the first group */
 	data->group = 1;
